Subject: odd timeouts, redux
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=openbsd-alpha&m=103051835227098

this evening has given me more time to check things out.

first, the network interface (fxp0) is probably the culprit. once the
interface goes down during heavy network load (nfs serving of /usr/src,
for example), it can be recovered through a simple ifconfig fxp0 [down |
up]. this seems to reset the buffer(s).. but, it is a far from ideal
solution for this problem. again, given some assistance, i'll gladly start
digging in to this, as far as i can.

an example of outgoing pings from the alpha:

	[jan@globalhead jan] {44}$ ping 192.168.1.100
	64 bytes from 192.168.1.100: icmp_seq=0 ttl=255 time=0.978 ms
	...
	64 bytes from 192.168.1.100: icmp_seq=57 ttl=255 time=3.908 ms
	ping: sendto: No buffer space available
	ping: wrote 192.168.1.100 64 chars, ret=-1
	ping: sendto: No buffer space available
	ping: wrote 192.168.1.100 64 chars, ret=-1
	ping: sendto: No buffer space available
	ping: wrote 192.168.1.100 64 chars, ret=-1
	...

this only happens intermittantly. from the NFS client side, the machine
simply stops responding to all network traffic for a while.

