From openbsd-alpha  Tue Aug 27 16:15:09 2002
From: "f.johan.beisser" <jan () caustic ! org>
Date: Tue, 27 Aug 2002 16:15:09 +0000
To: openbsd-alpha
Subject: odd timeouts..
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=openbsd-alpha&m=103046497404185

i've been using OpenBSD/alpha snapshots on my alphaPC 164 for a little
while. i've been finding, recently on a couple different kernels (GENERIC,
and my own custom kernel) that there've been odd timeouts during heavy
network usage. upon an attempted ping, i've been informed of insufficiant
buffer space, once.

my question for you, it would seem, is where to look to start solving this
problem.

nothing shows up in the alpha's dmesg.

on the console, the interface is reported correctly by the kernel (it's
up, active, and working).

sometimes, when sending an outbound packet, the interface is restored, and
everything recovers.

the amount of data seems to be arbitrary, but fully related to inbound
packets.

