   elsewhere?

Probably, yes.  The X support for VGA cards on the alpha is still very
experimental, so failures can be expected. But the Matrox driver is
one of those that I successfully tested last month.

In recent snapshots, I think I've introduced a problem that will
prevent the server from working when started by xinit or startx. On a
fresh system (ie GENERIC kernel) try to run just 'XFree86' as root. If
the X wave background and the X shaped cursor appear after a while,
then the X server is basically working. You can use xdm to start it. 

Otherwise, please send the contents of /var/log/XFree86.0.log. 

I'm going to try to fix those bugs before I leave for vacation, but I
don't promise anything. 


					Matthieu

